  "details": "Now that the VRChat camera has a SPOUT sender, and camera lense postions are already synced, it would be amazing if you could enable a setting to \"share\" your feed and make it accessible as a spout sender to other people. (Via a local camera that is position synced, not by streaming the actual video.)\n\nThis would allow live video production in VRChat to get a lot more advanced.\n\nE.g. You can have a multiple camera operators that move lenses and control perspectives, while you can grab and switch between these perspective feeds via separate spout senders.\n\n(e.g. vrcsender_FPaul)\n\nIdeally settings like Zoom and other are synced too, but even without, this would allow some crazy video works to be done live.",
